Tundra: Social post lifecycle

  Roles:
    - Author
    - Viewer
    - Moderator

  Relationships:
    - Author of Post
    - Viewer is Follower of Author

  Contracts:
    - Only the Author may create, edit or delete their own Post
    - A Post may be edited by the Author only while it is in Draft or Published
    - Only a Moderator may hide or remove a Post for policy violations
    - Any Viewer may react to or comment on a Published Post
    - Only a Follower of the Author may view a private Post
    - A hidden or removed Post is no longer visible to ordinary Viewers

  States:
    - Post is Draft
    - Post is Published
    - Post is Hidden by Moderator
    - Post is Removed by Moderator
    - Post is Deleted by Author

  Processes:
    - Create Post
    - Edit Post
    - Publish Post
    - Delete Post
    - Hide Post
    - Remove Post
    - React to Post
    - Comment on Post
    - View private Post

  Scenario: Happy path – author publishes a post
    Given no Post exists
    When the Author creates a Post
    Then the Post is Draft

    When the Author publishes the Post
    Then the Post is Published

  Scenario: Error – viewer tries to edit someone else’s post
    Given the Post is Published
    When a Viewer tries to edit the Post
    Then the edit is rejected
    And the Post remains Published
    And the contract "Only the Author may create, edit or delete their own Post" is broken

  Scenario: Moderator hides a post
    Given the Post is Published
    When the Moderator hides the Post
    Then the Post is Hidden by Moderator

  Scenario: Error – non-follower tries to view private post
    Given the Post is Published
    And the Viewer is not a Follower of the Author
    When the Viewer tries to view the private Post
    Then the view is rejected
    And the contract "Only a Follower of the Author may view a private Post" is broken
